# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/drafter-bf16 four-card window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/drafter-bf16 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-dbf16-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/drafter-bf16 commit; a commit of a file the image carries needs a new
# B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent, and deploys nothing.
# S1: the AUDITED smoke of the bfloat16 drafter on c2-packed-tp4-best-gate-dbf16 (every verify audit, the fused-commit audit and the singles audit on, QWEN_FAST_DRAFTER_BF16=1).
# READ (the smoke rule): exactly one '[DRAFTER_BF16] engaged' line per engine process, and NO '[PINDIAG] draft weights lent ... projections dtype=bf8' line anywhere (a bf8 lend line under the flag
# means the flag did not reach an upload); every audit line clean, mismatches=0; c2_smoke_check clean; no stall. The proposals differ from bf8's, so the [ACCEPT] mean may move, but the TEXTS of the
# verified output must equal best-gate's solo texts (the verifier decides every token): a text difference is a verification fault, not an acceptance effect. Record device DRAM free after attach
# (about 405 MB per chip less than the bf8 attach: the weights are shared by every drafter borrower, one copy). Stop rule: any marker miss, bf8 line, audit mismatch or stall stops the dbf16 arm (D1-D4 are skipped).
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min, engine build 10-30 min, the smoke 30-60 min: 100 min at most.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-dbf16-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-best-gate-dbf16
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady,steady_resend,concurrent4_code_equal
